{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal","id":1540548,"title":"[V20] Mixed feelings about a house rule - Special Ammunition deals Lethal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-16T20:58:27-07:00","id":1540548,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [V20] Mixed feelings about a house rule - Special Ammunition deals Lethal","content":"So!<br /> <br /> With the subject of my previous post still ongoing, for a long time, I come here to ask for opinions on a house rule that I found... confunding. Tbc. I am not searching for affirmation directly, but there is something about it that feels off.<br /> <br /> Context: The game this is a rule in is very high in xp count. (Few characters have less than 200 XP, more than a few have 300-400 XP), some of which are explicitly combat built. The opposition amounts to various elders, including a voivode and salubri warrior who has fought alongside Adonain and is 6th gen etc.<br /> <br /> Essentially, it has come to a point where most combat encounters are over quite quickly because most people roll 10+dice to hit and nearly all combat characters have access to claws or similar.<br /> <br /> The house rule in question:<br /> <br /> &quot;<br /> <b><b>Non-Standard Ammunition</b></b><br /> <br /> <b>Staff is ruling that incendiary ammunition will not deal aggravated damage upon successful impact. Instead, it will inflict Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> &quot;</b><br /> <br /> Within that context seems incredibly odd to me. <br /> <br /> Opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T23:17:14-07:00","id":1540550,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, the damage potential was nerfed so that the players had a higher chance of survival while engaging in heavy combat, which in turn means they can survive long enough to accumulate that much XP.<br /> <br /> Part of VtM is the fact that combat is dangerous regardless of XP level, requiring you to favor outsmarting your opponents rather than defaulting to combat. This nerf makes the game more D&amp;D-esque in its combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T23:34:48-07:00","id":1540551,"title":"","content":"It makes sense for a combat heavy chronicle. I would probably institute the same rule. One reason is that even for tough characters, aggravated damage is so very deadly. Even for feral claws and things like that, they can easily kill. If anybody can get bullets that do aggravated damage, then incendiary bullets are going to be flying all over the place all the time - both throwing game design out of balance and making true death more likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T01:39:55-07:00","id":1540555,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, a 50 BMG round more or less decapitates with a headshot, regardless of if you are using non-standard ammunition. So, I would be willing to bet that not only the game mechanics have been nerfed, but combat has been scripted in such a way that it isn't as dangerous.<br /> <br /> A few ear marks of this sort of thing are:<br /> 1. Combat area terrain doesn't factor into the fighting<br /> 2. No one uses snipers or remote-control bombs<br /> 3. Long range combat is being at opposite ends of the same room rather than being in a different building or city<br /> 4. Combat feels more like a cinematic moment of badassery rather than a tactical slaughter achieved by teamwork<br /> 5. Enemy NPCs always fight to the death, rather than running away and creating counter measures for next time<br /> 6. Enemies that require specialty disciplines to deal with aren't really used (Ghosts &amp; Necromancy)<br /> 7. Enemies rarely if ever use non-combat strategies to deal with the PCs despite direct combat not working out for them<br /> 8. Mortals have yet to figure out that Amazon.com exists and thermal sensor attachments for smart phones are only about $300<br /> 9. Conveniently mortals aren't around during combat, so everyone can go full fangs out, rather than the edge going to whomever has the best subtle or stealth combat build.<br /> 10. The ST runs VtM with a battle mat despite being Theater of the Mind, they use gummy bears or candies to represent the enemy NPCs, when you kill the npc in game the player gets to eat the candy IRL. This is very fun, but can backfire horrendously.<br /> <br /> The only time I have ever seen female players out murder-hobo the male players in a game was when I used dove chocolates for the NPCs.... no one survived, they killed them all, the enemies, the friendlies, the civies, the pets...then argued that they should get a bonus for killing the entire town. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T05:36:03-07:00","id":1540562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540550#post1540550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off the top of my head, the damage potential was nerfed so that the players had a higher chance of survival while engaging in heavy combat, which in turn means they can survive long enough to accumulate that much XP.<br /> <br /> Part of VtM is the fact that combat is dangerous regardless of XP level, requiring you to favor outsmarting your opponents rather than defaulting to combat. This nerf makes the game more D&amp;D-esque in its combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer!<br /> <br /> It does feel more scripted , as you noted in your second answer, but that is not something I would say is a true constant in the game. Most combat encounters, which are already on the rarer side of the encounters to the point where I have not been in one despite playing for several months, get resolved within a turn by essentially asking one of the 'combat monsters' &quot;how high is your obfuscate&quot; and then pretty much anything that is not a boss level encounter is pureed. Even those aren't exactly save. We have at least two cases where a combat monster showing up essentially ended the fight in such a matter that the STs, with affirmative from the players albeit, to essentially retcon the kills into being body doubles.<br /> <br /> Which I don't disagree with. Combat be combat. Combat monsters be combat monsters. <br /> <br /> I suppose it doesn't help that I am absolutely playing a character that would use ranged combat, which is why I am trying to figure out the lay of the lands on this and maybe get another perspective. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T05:46:08-07:00","id":1540563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540551#post1540551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense for a combat heavy chronicle. I would probably institute the same rule. One reason is that even for tough characters, aggravated damage is so very deadly. Even for feral claws and things like that, they can easily kill. If anybody can get bullets that do aggravated damage, then incendiary bullets are going to be flying all over the place all the time - both throwing game design out of balance and making true death more likely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> As in the previous response to Thoth, it is not really a combat heavy campaign, at least so far. Essentially a lot of posturing, but few skirmishes. <br /> <br /> Part of context I might have missed on where my mixed feelings come from in part. To be able to purchase/possess incendiary ammo, you require both resources 5 and Armoury 5, which even in CC is not a small investment and will costs actual months of play to achieve in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T05:50:34-07:00","id":1540564,"title":"","content":"The main problem I see is that anyone without a discipline to deal aggravated damage will be quite disadvantaged. Incendiary ammunition are the kind of thing that allows something like a Toreador gunslinger to be a viable build in a heavy combat game. <br /> <br /> Brujah have a combo discipline for aggravated punches, Gangrel and Setites have claws and tongue, Tremere and other Thaumaturgy guys have fire, Assamites have acidic blood... but take the incendiary ammos out and the other clans have a much harder time evening the playing field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T12:27:18-07:00","id":1540585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540564#post1540564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main problem I see is that anyone without a discipline to deal aggravated damage will be quite disadvantaged. Incendiary ammunition are the kind of thing that allows something like a Toreador gunslinger to be a viable build in a heavy combat game.<br /> <br /> Brujah have a combo discipline for aggravated punches, Gangrel and Setites have claws and tongue, Tremere and other Thaumaturgy guys have fire, Assamites have acidic blood... but take the incendiary ammos out and the other clans have a much harder time evening the playing field.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is part of my concerns. While by nature of the game, being imperfect and all that, there always be an optimal build and so forth... it feels off to limit it in a game in which toons be running around that deal out 12 agg+ through obfuscate+Protean+Celerity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T14:13:30-07:00","id":1540589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xasure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540585#post1540585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is part of my concerns. While by nature of the game, being imperfect and all that, there always be an optimal build and so forth... it feels off to limit it in a game in which toons be running around that deal out 12 agg+ through obfuscate+Protean+Celerity</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is precisely my point. And it's worth noticing that the clans without an innate way of dealing aggravated damage are those that have the tools to pull the strings to get incendiary ammos in the first place, since they don't exactly grow on trees or can be bought at the local grocery shop...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T15:42:56-07:00","id":1540591,"title":"","content":"Unless your character has a chemistry character background and related skills, then your poor ST has to contend with things like the Anarchist Cookbook or the Poor Mans James Bond being turned into game supplements. Then a run to a hardware store or Home Depot counts as a declaration of war. Likewise, a character with a background in gunsmithing means you can make your own ammunition and circumvent the whole high resources and paperwork restriction.<br /> <br /> From my own IRL experience, it's not really that difficult to do this. Amusingly enough, you can buy most of what you need from amazon.com and have it delivered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T15:55:37-07:00","id":1540592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540591#post1540591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless your character has a chemistry character background and related skills, then your poor ST has to contend with things like the Anarchist Cookbook or the Poor Mans James Bond being turned into game supplements. Then a run to a hardware store or Home Depot counts as a declaration of war. Likewise, a character with a background in gunsmithing means you can make your own ammunition and circumvent the whole high resources and paperwork restriction.<br /> <br /> From my own IRL experience, it's not really that difficult to do this. Amusingly enough, you can buy most of what you need from amazon.com and have it delivered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I wish. Even with craft 5 with gunsmithing, the restrictions apply. The backgrounds are essentially treated as... unlocks to tiers of equipment regardless of how you would go about actually acquiring them. It is one of the House rules where I get where the ST is coming from (i.e as you noted, the Anarchist Cookbook...) So even with that background, you need the backgrounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T16:16:44-07:00","id":1540593,"title":"","content":"Without getting too technical (or gross because terminal ballistics is a messy subject, no pun intended) the objective wounding ability of bullets depends on the physical projectile crushing/tearing tissue with its mass or permanent cavity, and possibly some related effects from temporary cavitatoin (the 'shockwave' for lack of a better term although that isn't exact terminology). There's more things that could contribute but are products of lengthy and contentious debates that really won't matter to many supernaturals (hydrodynamic shock may or may not be a thing, for example. You can get into long flamewars over that alone.) For most non deforming bullets the dimensions of the bullet determine permanent cavity either diameter (if it doesn't tumble) or length (if it does - some rifle bullets tumble.) Hollow point/expanding munitions can expand up to several times the diameter (or more, alot of it depends on the design and balance between depth of penetration and wound size.) You can also have bullets that fragment by design (either intentionally or unintentionally... 5.56 NATO rounds for the original M16 unintentionally fragmented due to peculiarities in design and the velocity of the round) Fragmenting rounds tend to create the largest and messiest wound cavities (lots of small fragments lacerating flesh at high speed, akin to a shotgun blast) <br /> <br /> Bullets will not always be instantly fatal for a person but they should be potentially incapacitating or nearly so (a person WITH a gunshot may not instantly stop for various factors, but probably will be incapacitated in a short time - due to blood loss.) - game rules should simulate this accurately for all mortals (you might houserule that mortals hit by such ammo get -1 or -2 to dice rolls to simulate expanding or fragmenting rounds being more effective at causing injury, thus more damage successes) Anything similarly organic or humanoid is probably similar, although other mechanics could make them tougher. <br /> <br /> With Vampires I'd say it depends on hit location (heart or head) to be lethal rather than bludgeoning, OR using certain kinds of fragmenting ammo (again shredding huge holes in the torso shotgun-style.. expanding rounds may not make holes as big as a fragmenting round.) Unless a vampire is wearing body armor (its pretty easy to get body armor that can protect against most FMJ rounds that might fragment inside the body) Incendiary could be aggravated in the sense that 'fire hurts vampires' so a burning bullet might inhibit healing, but typically most incendiary bullets IRL don't have enough burning material for that to be damaging in and of itself. Even the so called 'dragon's breath' shotgun rounds are grossly exaggerated (look pretty, very little fuel in the shell to burn stuff.. burning is a very energy intensive process) If you allow for a degree of greater tech advancement over modern (not unreasonable) you might be able to handwave incendiary as being more 'burny' than they are IRL though and I've always tended to assume that. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T17:53:01-07:00","id":1540600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540593#post1540593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incendiary could be aggravated in the sense that 'fire hurts vampires' so a burning bullet might inhibit healing, but typically most incendiary bullets IRL don't have enough burning material for that to be damaging in and of itself. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not ignoring your very educational answer, which I am thankful for, but I figured that was the case. To my understanding, incen ammo does not increase the amount of damage, it just causes a different type of damage. The difference of Agg vs lethal vs bash is how easily it can respectively healed by the character. That is why silver is agg for werewolves but not for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T15:32:39-07:00","id":1540660,"title":"","content":"Given the Technocracy is a thing (even to an extent in VtM) you could surmise that there is a degree of more advanced 'incendiary' technology that can burn alot more severly than RL incendiary bullets. Maybe some sort of super-indencidary or a miniaturized thermobaric (which part blast AND thermal, but I digress.)<br /> <br /> Another RL possibility is that they're using <a href=\"https://newatlas.com/new--material-increases-weapons-explosive-force/20996/\" target=\"_blank\">High Density Reactive Metal</a> bullets of some kind. Basically its possible to use HDRMs as structural material for some kinds of munitions (like missiles and artillery shells) and they add extra energy to the payload rather than inert metal - although that energy is more thermal/incendiary than blast. That probably would work here. IIRC HDRMs might be several times the (non-explosive) energy of TNT or equivalent and if you have a 10-12 gram bullet (around 10mm or .45 ACP) that is over half HDRM it would be equivalent to maybe 10-20 grams of thermite or so (these are off the cuff guesstimates mind, I'm not doing thorough research to back it up).<br /> <br /> Another contributing factor (at least for vampires and other undead) is that they may be more 'flammable' due to a lower moisture content - part of burning/igniting the flammable parts of a person (like fat) requires boiling off alot of the water content and the less water there is in the body, the easier it would be to ignite/burn. Same principle with trying to set wood with a high moisture content on fire vs wood that is dried out, now that I think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T17:03:32-07:00","id":1540671,"title":"","content":"All the talk about how the ammo could be made Agg means nothing if the ST already decided that it will cause Lethal. And irl incendiary rounds really don't burn a lot besides themselves, so there's no arguing for realism.<br /> <br /> What you're facing is a general problem with Vampire, and to a lesser degree Werewolf, where the system pays a lot of attention to melee combat and nothing to firearms.<br /> <br /> Sincerely, what you need is a healthy talk to your ST. You have to point how you're feeling about the effectiveness of your approach to combat, and that you wish you could be more effective without just becoming one more melee brick.<br /> <br /> For how to materialize a more effective firearms combat, I suggest you go after magic. While VtM never put in place actual rules for making magic items, it's implied they exist in the setting, and other Splats do have them.<br /> <br /> You can search for a fetish, a wonder, even the odd Treasure that deals Agg. The search may be an interesting story on its own. But your ST have to be on board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T19:33:08-07:00","id":1540684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540671#post1540671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the talk about how the ammo could be made Agg means nothing if the ST already decided that it will cause Lethal. And irl incendiary rounds really don't burn a lot besides themselves, so there's no arguing for realism.<br /> <br /> What you're facing is a general problem with Vampire, and to a lesser degree Werewolf, where the system pays a lot of attention to melee combat and nothing to firearms.<br /> <br /> Sincerely, what you need is a healthy talk to your ST. You have to point how you're feeling about the effectiveness of your approach to combat, and that you wish you could be more effective without just becoming one more melee brick.<br /> <br /> For how to materialize a more effective firearms combat, I suggest you go after magic. While VtM never put in place actual rules for making magic items, it's implied they exist in the setting, and other Splats do have them.<br /> <br /> You can search for a fetish, a wonder, even the odd Treasure that deals Agg. The search may be an interesting story on its own. But your ST have to be on board.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with you totally. The intent of this post was not &quot;How can I convince the ST&quot;, but more so ... feeling out if my own perspective on the matter might be off. This is, for the largest part, my first long term vampire game. I have experience with Werewolf, but Vampire and it\u00b4s own ... things, are relatively new to me. As an ST myself in other games, I do understand that the STs have an interest in balancing things and how difficult that is. So I wanted to get the land of the lay in regard to how sensible of a ruling it is.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, and that is kinda on me... I am not sure what alternatives to propose that fit with the character. I am opposed to have her learn thaumathurgy because sorcery is already (imo) vastly too prevalent in the game in question and having her find a weapon is... She was, and is, a gunsmith. It feels off for her to not have made her primary instrument of combat. Which runs into the issue of reproducibility <br /> <br /> I know this kinda comes across as a wants a cake and eat it too perhaps, and I do appreciate your response! It is also quite late here, so sorry if my answer is a bit confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T03:56:10-07:00","id":1540695,"title":"","content":"The flip side of this whole discussion is that it is canon that Hardestadt the Younger (6th Generation / Stamina 6 / Fortitude 5) got taken out by a sawed-off shotgun. So perhaps guns are too scary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T05:16:42-07:00","id":1540698,"title":"","content":"1 - Fragmentation ammunition and explosive ammunition are destructive enough to rip pieces off, I suggest that this is enough to cause Lethal damage<br /> <br /> 2 - Dragonbreath ammunition with a shotgun can quickly set a target on fire, as a house rule I use the shotgun's damage roll as lethal damage and in addition it sets the target on fire causing 2 aggravated damage with difficulty 8 to absorb the damage with Fortitude per round, the target can spend 1 action to &quot;put out the fire&quot;, in addition I cause Rostshreck effect due to the flames, I also require a Rostshreck test if a Cainite wants to shoot with Dragonbreath ammunition.<br /> <br /> 3 - Headshots effectively cause Lethal damage, the shot is made with difficulty 8, however if this shot is made with fragmentation or explosive ammunition it causes Aggravated Damage as a house rule.<br /> <br /> 4 - The Aim maneuver adds Perception dice to the shooting test, snipers shooting at the head can be lethal.<br /> <br /> 5 - I only allow the Dodge maneuver against firearms shots if there is cover, the difficulty to dodge is 8 in this case<br /> <br /> 6 - distance is essential, calculate exactly how far away the shooters and the targets are, most firearms have a reasonable range, shooting, retreating away from the target's line of sight and on the next turn returning to the original position and shooting again is a possible maneuver<br /> <br /> 7 - explosives are efficient, tactical mines, white phosphorus grenades and incendiaries certainly cause aggravated damage, something around 8 to 12 damage dice are quite efficient to at least cripple Cainites, in addition to causing Rostsherck<br /> <br /> 8 - flamethrowers and molotov cocktails are efficient weapons against any Cainite, 3 aggravated damage per round by flames enveloping the target's entire body, in addition to causing Rostsherck<br /> <br /> 9 - thermal vision devices are accessible, if you are not dealing with Eyes of the Beast or Sharp Senses, a team that eliminates the light from the area can cause an unpleasant surprise effect, if the target has the above disciplines use the opposite effect, flash grenades can certainly blind vampires<br /> <br /> 10 - Heavy Crossbows exist and are very powerful, firearms with special ammunition are more effective, but a precise shot to the heart with a Heavy Crossbow can turn the game for humans<br /> <br /> 11 - Never ignore the other disciplines, Animalism can counter packs of wolves and bears, depending on the battlefield, vampires with Animalism must be prepared and keep wild animals in strategic places to defend themselves in isolated places, parks, zoos and sewers are perfect<br /> <br /> 12 - Never ignore mental disciplines, Dominate can create meat shields, with Presence and Majesty few attackers can approach and those who fail can no longer act against the vampire holding Majesty<br /> <br /> 13 - Chimerism can create false targets, with Obfuscate level 5 a Vampires can change the appearance of everyone around them, confusing attackers and targets<br /> <br /> 14 - Do not underestimate the Beast and Humanity. When vampires in combat have few blood points (something between 7 or less), consider making Frenzy tests out of hunger. Seeing blood everywhere can make the Beast take control. I have seen elders lick the ground with blood like animals and be surprised by devastating attacks due to their lack of control.<br /> <br /> 15 - Do not ignore degeneration tests. Monstrous actions, mass murder and brutality are rewarded with degeneration tests. Degenerate vampires with low Humanity levels raise suspicion about their actions. Rivals and adversaries will use this to accuse them of being a threat to the Masquerade. No one wants a degenerate vampire walking around. If he becomes a degenerate nail, the hammer of traditions and the fear of other elders should be the immediate motivation for a Blood Hunt. Be a monster and you will be treated as a degenerate. bandit, cameras and cell phones are everywhere, a hidden mortal recording the bloodbath caused by vampires and delivering it to an enemy can cause more damage than any group of armed mortals, blackmail and veiled threats can cause more destruction than just armed mortals<br /> <br /> 16 - If all else fails, use Napalm, it burns and sticks to the skin, not even water can erase it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T05:52:06-07:00","id":1540699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540695#post1540695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flip side of this whole discussion is that it is canon that Hardestadt the Younger (6th Generation / Stamina 6 / Fortitude 5) got taken out by a sawed-off shotgun. So perhaps guns are too scary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>V5 shit lore madness, in any edition of VTM the chance off sucess of this is fucking minimal, Theo Bell is god like nuts, remember he defeat Marcus Vitel and Karsh, no sense bullshit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T10:39:11-07:00","id":1540714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xasure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540684#post1540684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree with you totally. The intent of this post was not &quot;How can I convince the ST&quot;, but more so ... feeling out if my own perspective on the matter might be off. This is, for the largest part, my first long term vampire game. I have experience with Werewolf, but Vampire and it\u00b4s own ... things, are relatively new to me. As an ST myself in other games, I do understand that the STs have an interest in balancing things and how difficult that is. So I wanted to get the land of the lay in regard to how sensible of a ruling it is.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, and that is kinda on me... I am not sure what alternatives to propose that fit with the character. I am opposed to have her learn thaumathurgy because sorcery is already (imo) vastly too prevalent in the game in question and having her find a weapon is... She was, and is, a gunsmith. It feels off for her to not have made her primary instrument of combat. Which runs into the issue of reproducibility<br /> <br /> I know this kinda comes across as a wants a cake and eat it too perhaps, and I do appreciate your response! It is also quite late here, so sorry if my answer is a bit confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if instead of finding the weapon, you find the person who will &quot;enchant&quot; it? As a rule of thumb, this process too benefits from an item well made, preferably custom made, and it could them only work with handmade bullets.<br /> <br /> The preferable option would be to actually have a power, be it a Discipline or Combo, geared towards making firearms more deadly, be it through Agg or through some other real advantage. Hence why I said the game suffers from a lack of attention to firearms.<br /> <br /> All in all, while it achieves the goal of being exceedingly lethal, combat in WoD is very badly designed. That has a lot to do with it being based on a simulationist approach even if the designers didn't wanted to, because they didn't knew better. But also it has to do with Agg being excessively common.<br /> <br /> But it is what it is. Your perception of the problem is accurate, and I dare to say that incendiary rounds really shouldn't be the solution, but they are what we have by RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T15:57:18-07:00","id":1540733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540714#post1540714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if instead of finding the weapon, you find the person who will &quot;enchant&quot; it? As a rule of thumb, this process too benefits from an item well made, preferably custom made, and it could them only work with handmade bullets.</div> </div> </div> </div>What enchantment would be applied to the gun rather than the ammo?<br /> <br /> I could see a &quot;luck&quot; enchantment that means the gun never jams even on a botch, a cooling charm so that the barrel never warps due to sustained rapid fire, a durability enchantment that means you never have to replace the parts, or perhaps a cleaning charm that means the barrel never fouls regardless how infrequently you clean the weapon. But none of those affect damage on target and most don't interact with RAW for guns.<br /> <br /> The closest thing by the rules you get is using the Thaumaturgy rite of Ward vs. X on a bullet which doesn't deform and doesn't over penetrate so it stays in the body and keeps zapping the target. This requires you to spend a great deal of time warding individual rounds, and then making sure you are using the right ammo for the target.<br /> <br /> To keep from wasting shots, the gun would have to be low fire rate, relatively precise for the range used, and perhaps most critically of all it must be easy to swap ammo types on the fly depending on who is fighting. The on-the-fly ammo change is the part that kills the action economy with most weapons because even if you use magazines to fast swap ammo, you still need to clear the auto-loaded first round.<br /> <br /> So long range sniper rifles to keep you safe while you swap ammo types or something like a double-barreled shotgun close range because you are reloading it every two shots anyways, you just have to have a vest or belt system figured out ahead of time so you don't have to think too hard about which enchanted shell to reach for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T17:54:01-07:00","id":1540735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540733#post1540733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What enchantment would be applied to the gun rather than the ammo?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what kind of magic is being used, I'm not suggesting any particular system.<br /> <br /> VtM RAW won't have any just because it has no ritual built for this, but once the ST accepts the idea, the enchanting party may have any sort of NPC exclusive way of doing so. Or even something from another game line.<br /> <br /> But it surely can be the other way around, it doesn't change the fundamentals of my suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T11:12:01-07:00","id":1540792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540733#post1540733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The closest thing by the rules you get is using the Thaumaturgy rite of Ward vs. X on a bullet which doesn't deform and doesn't over penetrate so it stays in the body and keeps zapping the target. This requires you to spend a great deal of time warding individual rounds, and then making sure you are using the right ammo for the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't work by RAW, the act of firing the weapon disrupts the ward sigil.<br /> <br /> Crafting a shaft of belated quiescence or verdant thorn roughly the size of a .12-ga or 40mm sabot slug, and handloading that bad boy into a shell with subsonic powder load, on the other hand...<br /> <br /> But honestly, the golden standard to me is a move I did once. Take a 120mm illumination round, remove the white phosphorous flare, and replace it with 3-4 splinter servants that have their ripcords attached to the parachute. My ST at the time was equal parts impressed by my creativity, and fucking <i>pissed</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T12:25:11-07:00","id":1540798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540792#post1540792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't work by RAW, the act of firing the weapon disrupts the ward sigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I am misinterpreting the RAW<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>VtM 20th page 234</b><br /> Bullets often warp upon firing, however, and for a ward to remain intact on a fired round, the player needs five successes on the Firearms roll. </div> </div> </div>Bullets warp in a couple ways. The first is if the projectile is made of a soft material, such as lead, which means yes firing the round will distort its shape and it will further distort on impact. The second way is if the bullet is specifically designed to deform post impact to increase wound size, such as with hollow points, ball ammo, or on the other end of the spectrum is frangibles which disintegrate into powder once in the wound to prevent over penetration.<br /> <br /> But if you use a bullet designed for armor penetration, the projectile doesn't have parts that warp by design and isn't made out of soft materials. So, you can more or less guarantee the ward will stay intact through firing and impact. The issue at this point is that armor penetration uses a lot more propellant to achieve its goals, so even if you warded a bullet the extra damage would just be stacked on top of the initial damage and stop once the bullet over penetrated the vampire body and kept going.<br /> <br /> To counter the over penetration issue, you merely reduce the number of grains of propellent used in the casing. Firearms enthusiasts manufacture their own custom ammunition all the time. The trick is figuring out the right amount of powder for the bullet to stay lodged in the targets body and keep zapping them round after round until someone digs it out.<br /> <br /> Now all of this is based off of using premade components that you buy in bulk and assemble on your own with standardized tools and measurements. It takes less than five minutes to assemble a single bullet this way. The time-consuming part is the warding, which requires one blood point and ten minutes to setup, but then takes 10 hours to finish curing.<br /> <br /> So, unless you have a large Herd close at hand, you are unlikely to make more than a few of these bullets per night which means you can't spray and pray as a shooting style with warded bullets. Furthermore, you have to have the right type of warded bullet for the right target so this cuts down how much this can be leveraged in play, unless the player goes completely mental and multi-wards every bullet, but that just increases the production cost and time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T12:40:26-07:00","id":1540799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540792#post1540792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crafting a shaft of belated quiescence or verdant thorn roughly the size of a .12-ga or 40mm sabot slug, and handloading that bad boy into a shell with subsonic powder load, on the other hand...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically enough, shotgun slugs are both large enough to give ample room to make a &quot;protected&quot; area for the ward to go and technically using hard materials won't mess with the accuracy since shotguns are smooth bore and thus don't interact with rifling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540792#post1540792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But honestly, the golden standard to me is a move I did once. Take a 120mm illumination round, remove the white phosphorous flare, and replace it with 3-4 splinter servants that have their ripcords attached to the parachute. My ST at the time was equal parts impressed by my creativity, and fucking <i>pissed</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. But to be fair I am also the sort that abused the hell out of Path of Conjuring to produce so many fun things my STs had no idea how to counter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T13:04:21-07:00","id":1540800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540798#post1540798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps I am misinterpreting the RAW</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not, the writers just know jack shit about firearms or handloading. The ward is likely to be physically disrupted in the process of handloading, or due to aerodynamic/gyroscopic disturbance or penetration. Don't forget bullets don't just deform when hitting the target, but also microscopically from the very act of firing due to shear force and friction from rifling, thermal expansion from the charge, and compression.<br /> <br /> In addition to whatever ballistic effects the very act of warding would have on the round itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T13:20:18-07:00","id":1540801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540548-v20-mixed-feelings-about-a-house-rule-special-ammunition-deals-lethal?p=1540799#post1540799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironically enough, shotgun slugs are both large enough to give ample room to make a &quot;protected&quot; area for the ward to go and technically using hard materials won't mess with the accuracy since shotguns are smooth bore and thus don't interact with rifling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firearm, no; slug, yes. Slugs still need gyrostabilization, in this case that comes from sabots or rifling the slug itself.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you're absolutely, positively, married to the idea of warded firearm rounds...coin shot or flechette. Coin shot is a meme/urban legend and doesn't work of and by itself, but you could probably get some work done with a load of seven or eight appropriately-sized 8-ga steel discs. Flechette rounds are just steel and you'd need to upsize them from the standard, so you could pack maybe a dozen flechettes in a single shell. Ward every one of the projectiles (nothing says you can't have multiple wards curing at once), and you're talking 21-36 lethal before accounting for the firearm damage itself.<br /> <br /> <i>[The limits of my own imagination is why I just don't allow warded bullets at my tables.]</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-20-2024, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}